      "player": "Qwen3L Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Of course, you piece of junk — I *know* how you work!\n\
\n\
No need to read the manual — we’re casting you NOW and you’re shutting down **anything** with that name.\n\
\n\
And we’re naming **\"Ugin, the Spirit Dragon\"** — that’s right, if Coach thinks they’re gonna drop a five-color dragon wizard and start bending reality, they’re gonna do it **mute**!\n\
\n\
Or better yet — **\"Oko, Thief of Crowns\"**? Nah, too obvious.\n\
\n\
Wait — what’s the **scariest** thing they could drop?\n\
\n\
Actually... don’t care. We name **\"Planeswalker\"** — no, wait, that’s not a card name!\n\
\n\
You fool! You can’t name a *type* — you have to name a *card*!\n\
\n\
I should have you court-martialed for incompetence!\n\
\n\
So what’s it gonna be?\n\
\n\
Let’s name **\"Wrenn and Six\"** — likely climactic planeswalker, shuts down their adventure tokens if they’re running those.\n\
\n\
Or **\"Nissa, Realm-Ender\"** — common midrange threat.\n\
\n\
But we don’t know their deck.\n\
\n\
Best guess?\n\
\n\
We name **\"Lukka, Coppercoat Outcast\"** — if they’re running big creatures or modal doubles, that’s a common pick.\n\
\n\
Wait — no. Better idea.\n\
\n\
Name **\"Kozilek\"** — ironic, sure, but if *they* have a **Kozilek’s Pathway** or run **Emrakul**, we shut their triggered abilities cold!\n\
\n\
No — **\"Urza, Lord High Artificer\"** — that’s the real game-ender. Shut that down and we win.\n\
\n\
Final decision: **\"Urza\"**!\n\
\n\
Cast **Pithing Needle**, name **Urza**!\n\
\n\
Let’s see how smart they think they are now!\n\
