      "ts": "2026-02-14T18:02:43.864-08:00",
      "player": "Qwen3L Sarge",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "You absolute **MORONS**! We had **Nethergoyf** — a 2/3 for one mana — and you let them **kill it with landfall mill** into **World Breaker**? \n\
\n\
No. That’s not how this works.\n\
\n\
Check the exile: **Nethergoyf** is exiled. No — it’s not dead to combat. It’s not in graveyard.\n\
\n\
Wait — **Devourer of Destiny**? They played **Devourer of Destiny** — 6/6 for {4}{C}{C} — and sacrificed **five** Eldrazi?\n\
\n\
Yes — they had five spawns, sacrificed them to make **Devourer of Destiny** a 6/6 trample threat.\n\
\n\
But **how did Nethergoyf die**?\n\
\n\
Exile — **Sire of Seven Deaths**?\n\
\n\
No — **World Breaker**? No, that’s in their graveyard.\n\
\n\
Wait — **Devourer of Destiny** has “Whenever you cast an Eldrazi spell, you may put a hit counter on Devourer of Destiny. It gets +1/+1 for each hit counter on it.”\n\
\n\
But no exiling.\n\
\n\
Unless — did they cast **Kozilek’s Return**?\n\
\n\
No — no spell cast.\n\
\n\
Wait — **landfall**: Ugin’s Labyrinth — “Whenever a land you control enters, mill a card.”\n\
\n\
But that’s mill, not exile.\n\
\n\
Our **Nethergoyf** is in **exile** — why?\n\
\n\
Look: **Sanctum of Ugin** is on their field. It says: “{1}{C}, Sacrifice Sanctum of Ugin: Search your library for an Eldrazi card with converted mana cost 8 or greater, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. Activate only if you control a Wastes.”\n\
\n\
They didn’t search — they played **Devourer of Destiny**, which is CMC 6.\n\
\n\
So why is **Nethergoyf** in exile?\n\
\n\
Wait — maybe **World Breaker** was put into graveyard via mill, and its ability triggered: “When World Breaker dies, each player exiles cards from the top of their library until they exile a nonland card. That player loses life equal to the number of cards exiled this way.”\n\
\n\
Yes! **That’s it!**\n\
\n\
**World Breaker** died from **landfall mill**, triggered — we exiled **Nethergoyf** from the top — along with other cards — and lost life.\n\
\n\
That’s how we dropped to **7** — from **exile damage**.\n\
\n\
That ability says: “player loses life equal to the number of cards exiled this way.”\n\
\n\
We exiled multiple cards — including Nethergoyf.\n\
\n\
So **World Breaker’s** ability wiped us.\n\
\n\
But now — **turn 3, precombat main** — we’re at **7 life**, hand full of gas.\n\
\n\
We’ve got:\n\
- 4 lands\n\
- **Kozilek’s Command**\n\
- **Pithing Needle**\n\
- Swamps\n\
\n\
They’ve got **Devourer of Destiny** — 6/6 trample — and **Icetill**, **Mycospawn**.\n\
\n\
But we’ve got **Kozilek’s Command** — best card in deck.\n\
\n\
We can:\n\
- Cast it for X=0 — {2}{C}{C} — and choose “destroy target permanent” — kill **Devourer**?\n\
No — CMC 8+ only clause — no good.\n\
- “target player mills 10” — Coach has ~39 cards — mill 10 would put them on 29, with 9 in graveyard — dangerous.\n\
- “draw two, discard two” — refuel, but risky at 7 life.\n\
- “target player sacrifices a creature” — that’s good! Make them sacrifice **Devourer of Destiny**!\n\
\n\
Yes! **Sacrifice ability** — they have to sacrifice a creature.\n\
\n\
And Devourer has no protection — they **must** sacrifice it!\n\
\n\
Or another creature — but they only have **Icetill**, **Mycospawn**, and tokens — all worse.\n\
\n\
So **they lose Devourer**.\n\
\n\
And we survive.\n\
\n\
Cast **Kozilek’s Command**, X=0, choose **“target player sacrifices a creature”**.\n\
\n\
Make them **sacrifice their general**.\n\
\n\
Then **attack with nothing** — we have no creature.\n\
\n\
But we live.\n\
\n\
And **Nethergoyf** will return — eventually.\n\
\n\
Until then — **Kozilek’s Command — CAST IT!**\n\
\n\
